Fri Oct 23 10:05:54 UTC 2026 - Tomasz Kantecki <tomasz.kantecki@intel.com>

- Update to v3.0.1:
  * Build system: removed legacy Makefile and Windows `.mak` builds; CMake is now the only supported build flow.
  * Build system: GCC and Clang builds now use the C11 standard.
  * Licensing: replaced full BSD-3-Clause license text in source files with SPDX identifiers.
  * OpenSSL: added `imb-provider`, an OpenSSL 3.x test provider supporting symmetric crypto, hash/HMAC and PQC operations, including asynchronous operation.
  * Self-tests: library initialization now fails closed on self-test failure, preventing cryptographic operations on the affected manager until successful reinitialization.
  * Architecture support: added AVX10 architecture support.
  * AES: added AVX2 Type 2 implementations for AES-CFB, AES-CBC, AES-CMAC and AES-CCM.
  * HMAC-SHA1: added variable tag sizes from 4 to 20 bytes.
  * SHA3/SHAKE: added SHA3-224/256/384/512, SHAKE128/256 and HMAC-SHA3 support, including optimized AVX2 and AVX512 implementations.
  * Zero-length messages: extended support across HMAC and AES-CBC algorithms.
  * 3GPP: added implementations of the new 256-bit confidentiality, integrity and combined algorithms based on AES, SNOW5G and ZUC.
  * DES/3DES: added a new common SSE Type 1 DES block encryption implementation.
  * PQC: added ML-DSA (FIPS 204) and ML-KEM (FIPS 203), including all standardized parameter sets.
  * CRC: added AVX2 Type 2 implementations using 256-bit VPCLMULQDQ polynomial folding.
  * Constant-time validation: added `CONSTANT_TIME_VALIDATION` build option for detecting secret-dependent branches and memory accesses using Valgrind.
  * Wireless algorithms: removed bit-length APIs and non-byte-aligned message length/offset support.
  * Direct APIs: removed direct API support for ZUC-EEA3/EIA3, SNOW3G-UEA2/UIA2, KASUMI-F8/F9 and CRC; these algorithms remain available through the job API.
  * Removed AES-CTR bit-length, AES-CBCS 1:9, SNOW-V/AEAD SNOW-V, ZUC-EEA3-256 and ZUC-EIA3-256 support.
  * Removed QUIC API, custom cipher and custom hash support.
  * API validation: added AES-CBC/AES-CFB message length checks and updated CFB APIs to return operation status.
  * Test applications: added `imb-safe-check` for detection of sensitive data left in registers and memory.
  * Test applications: added `imb-oob` for detecting out-of-bounds reads and writes using guard pages.
  * Test applications: expanded SHA3, SHAKE, ML-DSA and ML-KEM coverage across `imb-kat`, `imb-xvalid`, `imb-acvp` and fuzz testing.
  * Test applications: added ABI checking and improved zero-length message testing.
  * Wycheproof: moved Project Wycheproof coverage into `imb-kat`, updated to the upstream v1 vector set and removed `imb-wycheproof`.
  * Performance: added `imb-perf-cmp.py`, PQC benchmarking with `imb-speed-pqc`, SHA3/SHAKE and AVX10 support, and improved `imb-perf` stability.
  * Performance: renamed `ipsec_perf_tool.py` to `imb-perf-tool.py` and enhanced core selection and algorithm filtering.
  * Tools: added assembly formatting and coverage tools, plus source-file non-ASCII character detection and replacement.
- Fixed issues:
  * Fixed SM4-GCM plaintext/ciphertext address calculation (issue #159).
  * Fixed SNOW3G and KASUMI JOB API destination pointer calculation (issue #162).
  * Fixed SNOW-V-AEAD ciphertext address calculation (issue #161).
  * Fixed MD5-HMAC mapping in the performance application.
  * Fixed AES-GCM key structure alignment.
  * Fixed DES/3DES-CBC plaintext/ciphertext output (issue #169).
  * Fixed key pointer handling for AES-GCM, AES-GCM-SGL and SM4-GCM decryption.
  * Fixed PON XGEM PLI validation that could result in out-of-bounds memory access.
  * Fixed MinGW build issues (issue #185).
  * Fixed Windows GCC/MinGW stack alignment issue affecting ZUC-NCA6.
  * Fixed AVX10 architecture auto-detection.
  * Fixed GHASH job API out-of-bounds read for tag lengths below 16 bytes.
- More details at:
  * [intel-ipsec-mb v3.0.0 release](https://github.com/intel/intel-ipsec-mb/releases/tag/v3.0.0)

